ntion to these kind of rules but  like it's it's very open it's very very  accessible now and that's amazing and so  I'm like okay well I might as well try  this out what's the hum and Dad and I  did try it out and it was very easy and  it was very straightforward and all the  code you can build yourself and it's C  sharp C sharp is my favorite language  aside from C++ C was probably my my  favorite favorite language and the C  sharp is probably this my second  favorite language I haven't exactly used  C sharp extensively to write games I  mean I've obviously done some things  here and there using unity and I know C  sharp very well because back at EA we  used it for like all of our  windows-based tools which includes like  you know all the tools including a level  editor on like one of the engines I  worked at frostbites a frost ed let all  that editor's stuff is written in  c-sharp using WPF so I have a lot of  c-sharp experience because I was I was  mostly like a generalist of EA which  means that I basically did everything  and obviously a lot of game engine too  is the tools so I'm very familiar with  c-sharp I know a lot about its amazing  features amazing library it's a great  language and so that's what I did this  week I just slapped it into hazel the  first thing I did was actually put it  into hazel the public version like that  the public kind of hazel Trudy pushes  the game edge in the series the reason I  put it into that is because that's  obviously a smaller code base than hazel  dev which is with the 3d version of  hazel and I just thought that you know  let's start there so I basically looked  at various ECS systems oh we haven't  even talked about entity component  systems at all this video is dragging  out for so long  if you guys want to see more of this let  me know maybe I'll make more than one  with these videos a week or something  because I'm barely scratching the  surface of this telling you is a very  busy week long story short I jammed i